        "original_id": "633057d1-a711-5452-90f4-dc3ece0fa9d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ghana, Elubo, Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, Tema, Aflao\n- Roads: N1, National Highway 1\n- Topics: transport, geography\n\nFacts:\n- The N1, also called National Highway 1, is a national highway in Ghana.\n- The N1 begins at Elubo on Ghana’s border with Ivory Coast and runs through Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, and Tema to Aflao on Ghana’s border with Togo.\n- Winneba, traditionally known as Simpa, is a historic fishing port in southern Ghana.\n- Winneba lies on Ghana’s south coast, 90 miles east of Cape Coast.",
